GATE UPDATE!\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93Fridge Force drones attack\'94
\f0\b0 \strokec2 : final payoff. This one now needs substantive alignment. The current version has the Elvi sing until 
\f1\b \strokec2 \'93The gate opened\'94
\f0\b0 \strokec2 , after which they simply pass through. Under the emerging design, opening the decorative gates is insufficient: the invisible barriers are deadlier than the gates. The musical attack therefore has to derange or defeat the 
\f1\b \strokec2 access/security system deeply enough that the visible gates going down is the observable symptom of the invisible protection also ceasing to exclude the Elvi
\f0\b0 \strokec2 . This is the last contextual revelation: the pretty gates were never what had been keeping anyone out.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs26 \cf0 \strokec2 Fridge Force drones attack
\f0\b0\fs24 \strokec2  \'97 current gate failure is incompatible with the new fail-safe logic. Sensor disagreement cannot simply make the gates open. Treat that mechanism as stale. If the Elvi later breach the entrance, the cause must explicitly defeat/override 
\f1\b \strokec2 both
\f0\b0 \strokec2  the physical gate control and the invisible security. The song may accompany or contribute to that event, but it cannot merely confuse the system into failing open.\
\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

